  "worked_solution": "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.35$ | $0.1$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ | $0.55$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.55$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.45+1\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =-0.45+0.55 \\\\  & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.6+3\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =0.6+1.2 \\\\  & =1.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[6X+Y] & =6\\,\\text{E}[X]+\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =6(0.1)+1.8 \\\\  & =0.6+1.8 \\\\  & =2.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
